index 000000000..054ee5aef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0047-quote-discount-requests.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Quote-specific discount requests
+
+Approved product behavior: a buyer can request a discount on a received supplier quote now, or explicitly authorize Ahmad from Farq to send it one hour after confirmation. This is per received quote; it does not automatically enable discount requests for future quotes.
+
+Requests are persisted in construction.quote_discount_requests and linked to the exact current quote version and supplier invitation. A non-cancelled request is unique per quote version. Existing inbox correspondence handles channel selection, ownership, portal availability, provider dispatch, reply routing, audit, and idempotency. No second sender is introduced. The scheduled message records the automated persona, while retaining the authorizing colleague's user ID.
+
+The inbox worker executes due jobs only for its existing allowlisted companies. Scheduling is unavailable if worker, routing, or construction writes are disabled. Immediately before dispatch, current membership, role, request scope, correspondence ownership, quote version, RFQ version, and award/cancellation state are checked again. New inbound messages are protected by the existing parent-message guard. This may skip a scheduled discount and requires a human review.
+
+Jobs transition SCHEDULED → PROCESSING → SENT / FAILED / UNKNOWN / SKIPPED. Cancellation is atomic against claim. A stale PROCESSING job becomes UNKNOWN; it is never automatically resent. SENT means the existing correspondence path reports SENT, not that the supplier read or accepted the request. Discounts do not modify quote prices or award decisions; suppliers submit revised quote versions through the existing portal.
+
+Deployment requires the API migration, API and inbox-worker releases, and the companion farqconstraction UI. Local provider-mocked checks do not prove production delivery. No migration, message, credentials, billing, or messaging flags are changed in production by this implementation.
